[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3336442824","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103202#issuecomment-3336442824","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103202","id":3336442824,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7G3hPI","user":{"login":"jitspoe","id":7751182,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTExODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe","html_url":"https://github.com/jitspoe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-26T01:11:50Z","updated_at":"2025-09-26T01:11:50Z","body":"I tried to debug this while it was happening, but unfortunately the debugger froze the process long enough that the connections dropped, so I'm not sure if this is an accurate breakpoint or not, but this might be a clue:\n\n<img width=\"1011\" height=\"764\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/85e669a6-7e55-439d-a318-1e2d2b934df9\" />\n\nSeems the HTTPClient was in the STATUS_CONNECTED state, but the StreamPeerTLS connection was in the state STATUS_DISCONNECTED, which mad it set to STATUS_CONNECTION_ERROR and return ERR_CONNECTION_ERROR.\n\nCould be a legit disconnection, though.  This is a tough one to pin down because it requires leaving the project running for at least a day or two, sometimes more, and there's also the issue with a massive memory leak that ends up crashing a bunch of stuff on my computer: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/96598","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3336442824/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587314835","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103202#issuecomment-3587314835","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103202","id":3587314835,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7V0hST","user":{"login":"ColinSORourke","id":44822820,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODIyODIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44822820?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke","html_url":"https://github.com/ColinSORourke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ColinSORourke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T21:30:04Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T21:38:43Z","body":"@jitspoe I'm trying to see if I can reproduce this as well\n\nI created a Node that instantiates a child HTTPRequest, and makes a request to a known good endpoint on one of my websites every 8 seconds, and I'm going to let that run for a while and see if it starts failing ever.\n\nTo make sure I understand correctly, when you leave the project running for several days, at some point the Refresh_Token function begins consistently failing, by HTTPRequest.RESULT_CONNECTION_ERROR, repeatedly printing the failure warning `print_chat_window(str(\"Error refreshing token \", scope_type, \". Connection error.\"))`\nWhen you restart the program, it immediately succeeds again (with the exact same info I assume), so it's not a Connection Error from Twitch.\n\nOn your second comment - If I understand correctly, the HTTPRequest failure should be independent of either the HTTPClient or the StreamPeer because you are instantiating a new & independent HTTPRequest node for each Refresh_Token request, so it sounds like that's just the debugger slowing the process and causing your StreamPeer to drop regularly.\n\nDo you have any more info you can provide? Some things that could help:\n* Have you ever seen this occur on an HTTPRequest to any other URL?\n* Can you force it to occur faster by spamming unnecessary Refresh_Token requests?\n* Any data points on average time to fail, and number of HTTP_Requests made over that time? (E.G. 36 hours & 10 Refresh_Token requests)\n* Have you checked that your request data strings (client id and client secret) are still valid when the requests begin erroring out? I would add a print of those alongside the HTTPRequest.RESULT_CONNECTION_ERROR to verify the data has not corrupted in anyway when running for long periods of time.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587314835/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issu